    "body": "<!-- agent-note:v1 -->\nagent-note:v1 — state: done (fixed_merged)\nTask 17290 (lane code-b) complete: PR #7818 MERGED, merge commit 46f940565b4e7a888d35f03f96b7eda62d1012a2.\n\nWhat the shepherd pass did: rebased the single PR commit onto main 7551d098a5 (5 conflicted files resolved; ops.gen.ts regenerated — new OPERATION_FINGERPRINT 8560a42def; EffectExemptionPin 213→214 for the script.language exemption), then fixed all three Codex P2 findings on the reviewed commit, each replied to on its thread:\n1. Client selection matches shebang dispatch precedence — new runner.ClientScriptLanguage (shebang wins; explicit selection otherwise).\n2. Configured script.language now reaches API executions — execsvc.Limits.Language stamped by the daemon's ExecService() and the CLI's localService; Service.Run resolves effectiveLanguage = firstNonEmpty(opts.Language, s.Limits.Language) (explicit \"auto\" still overrides back to detection).\n3. CLI language resolves from the fully merged settings — resolved script.language beats a preset-loaded --language pointer; a command-line --language still wins (scanFlag).\n\nNew regression tests: TestClientScriptLanguage (runner), TestConfiguredLanguageAppliesToRuns (execsvc). Suites on the laptop: internal/runner, internal/api, internal/execsvc, internal/daemon PASS; go vet clean. Pre-existing failures verified identical on clean main and left alone: internal/settings TestTheEnvironmentDocIsCurrent + TestEveryDocumentHasAChapter, internal/cli TestInlineDaemonCancelledWhileWaiting (timing). Issue #1917 remains open — this PR was its deferred explicit-language remainder, not the whole epic.\n",
